---
import Layout from '../layouts/layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Coral Design System">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[560px]">
      <a
        href="#"
        class="inline-block text-[20px] font-medium text-text-primary-default hover:underline"
      >
        Type Scale EN
      </a>

      <article
        class="mt-2 rounded-sm border border-border-default-subtle bg-bg-surface-base px-7 pb-7 pt-6 shadow-[0_1px_0_rgba(16,24,40,0.02)]"
      >
        <header class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-tight text-text-default-muted">
            Coral Design System 2.0
          </p>
          <div class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </header>

        <h1
          class="mt-1 text-[38px] leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-text-default-high-contrast"
        >
          Spacing Guidelines
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-3 text-[12px] leading-[1.45] text-text-default-muted">
          The spacing system provides a scalable, grid-aligned foundation that unifies typography,
          components, and layouts. It helps designers and developers maintain visual rhythm, improve
          readability, and achieve consistent spatial structure across screens.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[12px] leading-[1.45] text-text-default-muted">
          All spacing values, paddings, gaps, and layout grids are based on a px baseline grid.
          Every value must be a multiple of 4 to ensure predictable alignment between text,
          components, and surfaces.
        </p>

        <hr class="my-6 border-border-default-subtle" />

        <h2 class="text-[26px] leading-[1.2] font-semibold text-text-default-high-contrast">
          Base scale
        </h2>

        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[520px] border-collapse text-left">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle text-[11px] text-text-default-muted">
                <th class="pb-2 font-medium">Token</th>
                <th class="pb-2 font-medium">Value (px)</th>
                <th class="pb-2 font-medium">Component</th>
                <th class="pb-2 font-medium">Usage</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-[11px] leading-[1.45] text-text-default-default">
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-1</td><td>4 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Micro spacing for icon gaps, helper text, and minor UI adjustments.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-2</td><td>8 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Tight component padding (chips, small controls) and compact layouts.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-3</td><td>12 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Compact separation between small text blocks or grouped items within the same
                  component.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-4</td><td>16 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Default component padding for cards, form fields, and general internal spacing.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-5</td><td>20 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Balanced vertical spacing in sections with medium information density.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-6</td><td>24 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Separation between unrelated components or content groups for medium content
                  density.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-7</td><td>28 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Wide block spacing between section rows, groups, or data panels.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-8</td><td>32 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Standard padding for containers, sections, or cards at desktop scale.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-9</td><td>36 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Page-level spacing for large sections or surface boundaries on wide screens.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-10</td><td>40 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Large section spacing for page layouts and component clusters.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr class="border-b border-border-default-subtle"
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-11</td><td>48 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Major vertical rhythm break to separate content zones.</td
                ></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><td class="py-2">space-lg-12</td><td>64 px</td><td>•</td><td
                  >Full-width page padding or major layout breaks in dense desktop canvases.</td
                ></tr
              >
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .logo-mark {
    position: relative;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }

  .logo-mark::before,
  .logo-mark::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: var(--color-text-primary-default);
  }

  .logo-mark::before {
    width: 8px;
    height: 18px;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
  }

  .logo-mark::after {
    width: 18px;
    height: 8px;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
